*The Giant gestures slowly, speaking in measured, reverberating tones*

The coordination... is happening... again.

I will tell you three things.

**One.** The tests... they speak of a cart. Items. Quantities. Totals. Listen to what they whisper.

**Two.** The implementation must be pure. Only what is needed. No more.

**Three.** Here is the way:

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items map[string]*Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: make(map[string]*Item),
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	if existing, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		existing.Quantity += quantity
	} else {
		c.items[name] = &Item{
			Name:     name,
			Price:    price,
			Quantity: quantity,
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	delete(c.items, name)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) UpdateQuantity(name string, quantity int) {
	if item, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		if quantity <= 0 {
			delete(c.items, name)
		} else {
			item.Quantity = quantity
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItem(name string) *Item {
	return c.items[name]
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []*Item {
	result := make([]*Item, 0, len(c.items))
	for _, item := range c.items {
		result = append(result, item)
	}
	return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = make(map[string]*Item)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) ItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) IsEmpty() bool {
	return len(c.items) == 0
}
```

*The Giant raises a finger slowly*

One and the same. Remember this.

The `ShoppingCart` holds `Item` entries by name. When adding, if the name exists, quantities merge. The total multiplies price by quantity across all items. `UpdateQuantity` with zero or less removes the item entirely. `ItemCount` sums all quantities, not unique items.

*Long pause, lights flicker in the White Lodge*

The tests require only this. No discounts. No taxes. No persistence. The owl is not what it seems... but the implementation is exactly what the tests demand.

Nothing more must be added. The path is narrow. Walk it precisely.

*The Giant fades into static*
